# Fix the whole class, not the example

When the owner reports a bug, wrong score, wrong filter, missing case, or “we missed X”:

1. **Treat the cited ID/UI as a repro**, not the full scope. Find the underlying rule/heuristic and fix that.
2. **Worldwide / catalog-wide fix** — an example unit, OP, pilot, or stage is never a license to special-case that id. Fix every entity that shares the same master signal, code path, or condition shape.
3. **Do not** ship ID-specific special cases (`if uid == "1370005900"`) unless master data is truly unique and there is no general signal.
4. **Double-check breadth before calling it done:**
   - Scan the full catalog / same code path for other hits (same pattern, same field, same board).
   - Report counts: how many were wrong, how many still correctly fail, example names.
   - Prefer a one-off script or assertion over eyeballing one unit.
5. **After the fix**, verify the original repro *and* at least one other affected case (or confirm the scan shows zero remaining false positives of that class).
6. If a true one-off is unavoidable, say so explicitly and why a general rule cannot cover it.

Owner reminder (Aug 2026): “when I give you an example of a bug, check and make sure it is a worldwide fix and not a particular fix.”
